course: dictionary
lesson: 6783
title: A short word with a long story
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are short forms of longer words. «Orang» on its own is a short form of orangutan, the large red-haired ape that lives in the forests of Borneo and Sumatra. Look at the words around it: if a text talks about apes, trees and rainforests, then orang most likely means orangutan.
explain: Read this: «Orangutan babies stay with their mothers for about 7 or 8 years, longer than any other animal except humans.» The clues are babies, mothers and years, so the word is about a living creature, not a place or a thing. You can see orang at the start of orangutan.
explain: Orang is also a Malay word meaning «person» or «people». Orangutan means «person of the forest» in Malay. Orang is not related to the colour orange, even though the two words look alike. Check the clues before you decide which meaning fits.
fact: Orang is a short form of orangutan, a large red-haired ape.
fact: Orangutans live in trees in Borneo and Sumatra.
fact: In Malay, «orang» means «person» or «people».
fact: Orangutan means «person of the forest» in Malay.
fact: Orang is not related to the colour orange, though the spellings look alike.
exercise: Orang is a short form of which word? | *orangutan | orange | orchestra | organ
exercise: «Orangutan babies stay with their mothers for about 7 or 8 years.» What kind of animal is an orangutan? | *A large red-haired ape that lives in trees | A tall bird that sings at dawn | A fruit like an orange
exercise: In Malay, «orang» means what? | Colour | Forest | *Person or people
test: Is orang related to the colour orange? | *No, they are different words | Yes, orang means orange in Malay | Sometimes, depending on the sentence | Yes, it is a shade of orange
test: Which places do orangutans live in? | *Borneo and Sumatra | Africa and Antarctica | Iceland and Norway | Spain and Italy
exam: In Malay, what does «orangutan» mean? | Ape | *Person of the forest | Red hair | Tree house
